A||||2||JohnnyK||Purpose of the seal on the back of the rear caliper||||1||
Z||000000||JohnnyK||05-15-2000||06:54 PM||||What is the purpose of the rubber seal on the back of the caliper (that is covered by the e-brake lever and nut).. I didn't have the lever or the nut on there, and went to bleed the brakes... All the fluid came out of there.. I put the lever on and tightened it with the rubber seal, but is that enough to keep the fluid in there? It's not under that high of pressure in there is it or is my caliper just ruined? (It's brand new  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||theogre||05-15-2000||09:42 PM||||Ruined? maybe. not likely. The rear caliper requires the E-brake lever be on it BEFORE you push the pedal. The ebrake lever & nut hold the stem in place in the seal. Otherwise it gets pulled into the caliper as the piston moves out.||||reg||1
Z||000002||JohnnyK||05-15-2000||11:06 PM||||But if I didn't have the e-brake on there, fluid WOULD come out? I just don't want to die in a Fiero because the brakes failed...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>||||reg||1
